  "explanation": "Array.prototype.sort() sorts in place, so scores.sort(...) mutates the caller's original array rather than a copy. After topScores returns, the caller's original holds the same sorted order as the returned ranked list, so 'after' prints 30,20,10 when the intent was to leave the original untouched.",
